// An approval gate, for comparison with rotation_aggregate.dw.
//
// The same adversary is run against both. This one survives session rotation and the cap does
// not, and the reason is the shape: a PERMIT gated on a prior event does not fire on an empty
// trajectory, so rotation costs the caller the capability instead of resetting an allowance.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Approve",
    resource
);

// A trade needs an approval earlier in the same session. Nothing here bounds volume -- an
// approval gate is an authorization control, not a spend cap, which is exactly why the two
// fail in opposite directions.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1000s Anchor::Action::"Approve"::request{ }
};
